# Privacy and security


::divider{aqua}
## What stays on your computer

Documents, notes, sheets and drawings are kept in your browser or in files you choose. The apps do not upload them, and there are no accounts to make for ordinary use!

## What goes online, and only when you ask

* **Share & Chat, Overshare, Phosphor, Antimony, Beta, Mintcode and Yuzu mail** send what you put in them to their own servers, because that is how they work!
* ++T~Pictures from OpenDB++ are fetched from this site when you insert them!
* ++T~Math++ is drawn by KaTeX, which is bundled with the site!

## How the site protects itself

* ++B@]Security headers++ on every page: no other site can frame Radii Office, and scripts and styles come from known places!
* ++B@]Signed downloads++ with published keys and fingerprints in `/signing/`!
* ++B@]Integrity hashes++ on loaded scripts, so a changed file is refused!
* ++B@]Safe Keydown.++ Text drawn by Keydown in shared places (messages, posts, mail) is cleaned again after it is drawn, so scripts and frames in it are removed!
* ++B@]Mail content.++ Real email in Yuzu is shown inside a sandboxed frame with a strict policy, and pictures from the internet are blocked until you press !!#PR#Load pictures#!

## Reporting a problem

If you find a security problem, please tell the team using the contact link on the [home page](/) before posting it publicly. The code of conduct is [here](/code-of-conduct)!

## Licenses

The suite is free software. OpenDB content is CC0 (public domain), and fonts and icons keep their own free licenses, listed in `ATTRIBUTIONS.md` and `ATTRIBUTIONS-FONTS.md` in the source!
